Additional third-party dependencies (imported libraries) are declared in
pyproject.toml under [project.dependencies] and [project.optional-dependencies].
They are installed by the user, not redistributed with MalValid, and each is
under its own license (see each package's metadata). Most are MIT, BSD or
Apache-2.0; some transitive dependencies are not, for example tqdm (MPL-2.0 AND
MIT), typing_extensions (PSF-2.0), shellingham (ISC), and, on Linux,
nvidia-nccl-cu12, a proprietary NVIDIA library that xgboost pulls in. Check
these before redistributing an environment or container image.

The fragments in docs/_notice/ contain detailed third-party attribution per
agent.
